Subject: The cached add-transition replay does not add to a prototype

What this does
  - `regvm_put_field_add_hit` returns a miss for a receiver that is a prototype, so the generic add
    makes the store.

Why we need it
  The generic add of a property to a prototype moves the prototype watchpoint epoch (`add_property`), and
  so `aot_pic_epoch`: cached lookups that went through the prototype are no longer trusted. The replay of
  a cached add transition changes the receiver's shape without going through `add_property`, so it did
  not move the epoch when the receiver was a prototype. Compiled code that tests its prototype holders
  once per epoch rather than per access needs every addition to a prototype to move it. The replay is for
  the common case of adding to an ordinary object; an addition to a prototype is rare and takes the
  generic path.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -25115,6 +25115,9 @@
         return 0;
     if (!p->extensible || p->is_exotic)
         return 0;
+    /* a property added to a prototype is the generic add's to make: it moves the watchpoint epoch */
+    if (unlikely(p->is_prototype))
+        return 0;
     if (e->misses != (uint16_t)ctx->rt->ic_watchpoint_epoch)
         return 0;                   /* a prototype interceptor appeared */
     nsh = b->regvm_pic_holder[b->regvm_pic_count + site];
